{"url": "https://math.uga.edu/how-apply", "final_url": "https://math.uga.edu/how-apply", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-29", "text": "How to Apply | Department of Mathematics\nSkip to main content\nSkip to main menu\nSkip to spotlight region\nSkip to secondary region\nSkip to UGA region\nSkip to Tertiary region\nSkip to Quaternary region\nSkip to unit footer\nHeader\nDepartment of Mathematics\nMenu\nMini menu\nGive Now\nSearch\nSearch this site\nSubmit Search\nClose\nUniversity of Georgia\nMain menu\nUndergraduate\nMajors\nMinors\nDouble Dawgs Program\nTransfer Students\nExperiential Learning\nAdvising\n>>\nMath Advising\nUndergraduate Research\n>>\nGraduate Students DRP Mentors\nUndergraduate Research Faculty\nUndergraduate Activities\nUndergraduate Student Resources\n>>\nFinal Graduation Steps\nUndergraduate Awards\nGraduate\nGraduate Degree Programs\nGraduate Student Forms\nGraduate Handbook\n>>\nDegree Requirements\nRegistration Requirements\nProgress Guidelines\nTeaching Assistants\n>>\nTeaching Guidelines\nGrievance Procedures\nGraduate Course Listing\nGraduate Advising\nProspective Graduate Students\n>>\nHow to Apply\nGraduate Courses\nCurrent Graduate Students\n>>\nCurrent and Former PhD Students\nGraduate Student Seminar\nGraduate Students Awards\nPast Graduate Student Seminars\nGraduate Qualifying Exams\nAbout\nWhy Major in Mathematics?\nHistory of Mathematics at UGA\nContact\nVisitors\n>>\nVisitor Information\nVisit the Department\nMake a Gift\nMath Department Merchandise\nCourses\nUndergraduate Courses\nMath 1113 Home Page\n>>\nMath 1113 Grading and Attendance Policy\nMATH 1113: Testing and Homework Information\nMath 1113 - Midterm and Final Exams\nMATH 1113 Intensive\nMath 1113 Help Information\nMATH 2250 Home Page\n>>\nMath 2250 Course Information\nMath 2250 Final Exam Info\nMath 2250 Help\nUndergraduate Honors Courses\nDepartmental Syllabi\nStudy Hall and Tutoring\nResearch\nSeminars\nAll Seminars\nAlgebra\nAlgebraic Geometry\nAnalysis\nApplied Math\nGeometry\nFunctional Analysis and Applications seminar\nGraduate Algebraic Geometry Seminar\nGraduate Student Seminar\nGraduate Topology and Algebraic Geometry Student Seminar\nM.A.L.T. Seminar\nMath Colloquium Schedule\nNumber Theory/Arithmetic Geometry\nSMARTS\nTopology\nNews & Events\nNews\nUpcoming Events\nPast Events\n>>\nPast Cantrell Lectures\nPlacement\nMath Placement Exam (DMAT)\nALEKS Placement\nAdvanced Placement Credit\nTransfer Credit\nRemedial Assistance\nFaculty Resources\nFaculty/Personnel Login\nReserve a Room in Boyd\nDirectory\nDepartment Leadership\nFaculty\n>>\nProfessors\nAssociate Professors\nAssistant Professors\nLimited Term Assistant Professors\nAcademic Professionals, Lecturers, Instructors\nPostdoctoral Associates\nAdjunct\nRetired Faculty\nStaff\nGraduate Students\n>>\nGraduate student DRP mentors\nUniversity Awards\n>>\nMathematics Department Award Winners\nAlumni\nHow to Apply\nThe deadline for Fall admission with full consideration for all possible financial aid is January 1. Applications completed after that date will still be considered for admission but will miss some financial aid opportunities. The department normally does not admit students for Spring semester, as both our assistantship budget and our program of courses are geared toward Fall admissions.\nWe do not require GRE scores for applicants to our Graduate Program, but you may report your scores if you would like them to be considered.\nAll our PhD students receive 5 years of full financial support. Applied Math alert! We currently have several generous grant-funded research assistantships (no teaching assistantship duties) available on a competitive basis for excellent PhD students committed to working in applied mathematics.\nTo apply for admission, please send the following items to the appropriate location:\nSubmit the following supplemental form to the Department of Mathematics:\nDepartment Background and Interest Form\n(Please note: We will only consider applicants that apply both through UGA's Grad School and submit the form above. If you're unable to access this form, please email Math Graduate Advising and Admission to let us know before 12/18 )\nSubmit the following with your online application to the Graduate School:\n1 unofficial copy of transcripts (Graduate School instructions)\nStatement of Purpose (include your name)\nOfficial TOEFL or IELTS scores (for international students)\nThree letters of Recommendation - electronic submission after application completion\nList of college math courses, grades received, textbook used (if known), and overall math GPA (see instructions)\nApply Now\nSidebar:\nNeed more info?\nContact our Grad Programs Team (consisting of Paul Pollack and Jimmy Dillies) : grad@math.uga.edu\nMain menu\nGraduate Degree Programs\nGraduate Student Forms\nGraduate Handbook\nGraduate Advising\nProspective Graduate Students\nHow to Apply\nGraduate Courses\nCurrent Graduate Students\nCurrent and Former PhD Students\nGraduate Student Seminar\nGraduate Students Awards\nPast Graduate Student Seminars\nGraduate Qualifying Exams\nSupport us\nWe appreciate your financial support. Your gift is important to us and helps support critical opportunities for students and faculty alike, including lectures, travel support, and any number of educational events that augment the classroom experience. Click here to learn more about giving.\nEvery dollar given has a direct impact upon our students and faculty.\nDepartment of Mathematics\nBoyd Research and Education Center\nUniversity of Georgia\nAthens, GA 30602\nPrivacy Policy\nLogin for Faculty,Staff and Students\nmath-web@franklin.uga.edu\nPhone:\n706-542-2211\nFax:\n706-542-5907\nlinkedIn\nSchools and Colleges\nDirectory\nMyUGA\nEmployment Opportunities\nCopyright and Trademarks\nPrivacy\nWebsite Feedback\nReport an Accessibility Barrier\nHuman Trafficking Notice\nReporting Hotline\n\u00a9 University of Georgia, Athens, GA 30602\n706-542-3000\n#UGA 